  "instructions": [
    {
      "id": 0,
      "kind": "prep",
      "primary_message": "Pick the parsley leaves from the stems and finely chop them. Mince the shallot. Core and cut the Roma tomatoes into 1/4-inch thick slices. Remove the tops and core from the fennel bulb. Thinly slice the mortadella. Thinly slice the Genoa salami. Thinly slice the provolone cheese. Thinly slice the hot capicola. Remove the stems from the pepperoncinis, then cut them into ¼-inch slices. Wash and dry the romaine lettuce.",
      "secondary_message": "¼ cup flat leaf parsley\n1 medium shallot\n5 Roma tomatoes\n½ fennel bulb, slice paper thin\n0.23 kg mortadella\n0.23 kg Genoa salami\n0.23 kg provolone cheese\n0.23 kg hot capicola\n10 pepperoncinis\n5 leaves romaine lettuce"
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "primary_message": "In a large bowl, whisk together olive oil, red wine vinegar, balsamic vinegar, parsley, shallot, oregano, and red pepper flakes. Season heavily with salt and pepper.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "primary_message": "Add in red onion, tomatoes, and fennel. Toss to thoroughly coat vegetables in vinaigrette. Let vegetables rest in vinaigrette for 20 minutes, tossing again halfway through. Strain vegetables into a bowl and reserve remaining vinaigrette.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "primary_message": "Open up bread and layer on mortadella, salami, provolone, and hot capicola. Top with marinated vegetables, pepperoncinis, red peppers, and lettuce.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "primary_message": "Light one chimney full of charcoal. When all the charcoal is lit and covered with gray ash, pour out and spread the coals evenly over entire surface of coal grate. Set cooking grate in place, cover grill and allow to preheat for 5 minutes. Clean and oil the grilling grate. Place bricks on grill, cover grill and let fire cool down to medium-low, between 300-163°C (150-165°C). Transfer sub to grill and place a large sheet pan on top of sandwich. Wearing well insulated grilling gloves, carefully balance bricks on sheet pan. Cover grill and cook until cheese has started to melt and sandwich has flattened, about 15 minutes. Remove sandwich from grill, slice into 4 to 6 portions and serve with reserved vinaigrette.",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
